# Events

**Color:** `#FDCB6E` | **Nodes:** 6

The Events category provides nodes that respond to runtime events such as application start, timer ticks, key presses, and property changes.

## Core

**Color:** `#FDCB6E`

### Begin

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/begin` |
| **Node Name** | Begin |
| **Description** | Fires once when the graph evaluation starts. Useful for initializing values, setting up state, or triggering an initial computation chain. |

**Inputs** — none

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `started` | Bool | Emits `true` once on startup |

**Example Usage**

```
[Begin] → [Constant] setup    // Initialize values on startup
```

### Tick

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/tick` |
| **Node Name** | Tick |
| **Description** | Fires every frame/update cycle. Provides delta time and total elapsed time for animation, physics, or real-time data processing. |

**Inputs** — none

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `deltaTime` | Float | Time since last tick in seconds |
| `elapsed` | Float | Total elapsed time since graph start |

**Example Usage**

```
[Tick] → [Sine Wave] → [Gauge]          // Animate based on elapsed time
[Tick] → [Integrator] → [Counter]       // Accumulate delta time
```

### Timer Event

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/timerEvent` |
| **Node Name** | Timer Event |
| **Description** | Fires at a configurable interval. Useful for periodic checks, sampling sensors, or scheduling repeated actions. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `interval` | Float | `1.0` | Interval in seconds between firings |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `fired` | Bool | Emits `true` each time the interval elapses |
| `count` | Float | Number of times the timer has fired |

**Example Usage**

```
[Timer Event] → [Read File] → [Display]     // Poll a file every 5 seconds
   interval: 5.0
```

### Input Event

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/inputEvent` |
| **Node Name** | Input Event |
| **Description** | Responds to external input events (keyboard, mouse, system events) by type. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `eventType` | String | `""` | Event type to listen for (e.g. `"keyPress"`, `"mouseClick"`) |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `triggered` | Bool | Emits `true` when the event occurs |
| `data` | String | Event payload data |

### Signal Event

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/signalEvent` |
| **Node Name** | Signal Event |
| **Description** | Listens for a named signal from Qt's signal/slot system and fires when the signal is received. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `signal` | String | `""` | Signal identifier to listen for |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `received` | Bool | Emits `true` when signal is received |
| `value` | Generic | Optional payload from the signal |

### Property Changed

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `events/core/propertyChanged` |
| **Node Name** | Property Changed |
| **Description** | Monitors a named property for changes and fires when the value updates. Useful for reacting to UI state changes or external data updates. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `property` | String | `""` | Property name to watch |
| `value` | Generic | — | Current property value (read) |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `changed` | Bool | Emits `true` when property changes |
| `newValue` | Generic | The updated value |

**Example Usage**

```
[Slider] → [Property Changed] → [Multiply] → [Display]   // React to slider changes
```
